 | L32 | **Confirming a SIM swap, or setting up the owner number (P2-2w d2b; CH-1, CH-7, CH-19).** While the owner line is swapped or unbound and the bridge reads the modem's SIM serial, the signed-in home page shows the note (now ending "below") and a form: "Use the SIM ending in NNNN for my number", a warning to do it only for a SIM the owner put in, and a code field that takes a code-generator code or the asked grid cell. **A code is always asked, also within `FreshFor`** (stricter than RESUME): adopting re-opens the owner channel on that SIM's line, so a SIM swapper holding a fresh session on a phone still needs a code they do not hold (CH-19). The unlock proof is refused. The page never sees the serial: `page_line` carries an opaque tag (the first 8 bytes of SHA-256 over "agentos sim " and the serial, hex) and the last four digits; agentosd adopts only the SIM whose tag matches what the bridge reports now, so a SIM changed after the page loaded is refused as stale. agentosd records the serial as `owner_iccid` in `-modem-roles` (`/var/lib/agentos/modem/roles.json`, other keys kept, 0644, replaced by rename), and the bridge takes it at its next open (within `Retry`, 10 s). **Carry:** P2-1's image must make `/var/lib/agentos/modem` writable by agentosd's user and readable by `agentos-modem` (no agentosd unit is in the repo yet); until then a refused write is "I can't answer right now" and nothing changes. A SIM whose serial cannot be read cannot be adopted (the note says to check the SIM). The box's own number (BOX_NUMBER, AT+CNUM) is not touched. No overlap with P2-2w c2: setup's ops record no modem roles. | CH-1, CH-7, CH-19 | A bridge-side refusal of adoption, if the bridge must veto agentosd's record, would need a writable roles directory in its unit, which L3 on #170 ruled out. |
 | L33 | **The Forget page (W3-forget-b3r, potency R2 of W3-forget-b3).** `/forget/`, behind sign-in, lists the owner's recent tasks from agentosd (`page_forget_tasks`, tokened) by FORGET's own labels, each escaped inside `<bdi>`, with an "Ask to forget" form that posts the goal ID alone to `/forget/ask` (POST only, same-origin, `s.post`). The form's token is an HMAC over the phone's sign-in and the task ID, so another phone's or an edited form is stale and asks nothing. agentosd (`page_forget`, a live token) asks only for a task it still lists and only while the session is unlocked; both ops take "unlocked" from the same status read that checked the token's lock generation (SR3-1), so a lock and re-unlock between reads cannot pass "unlocked" to an older session; the owner then approves the request with a code, so the page says "asked" and never that a task is forgotten. A locked session shows no labels. agentosd's failures are fixed page text. | CAP-3, CH-7, CH-8 | `cmd/agentosd` P1–P4. |
 | L34 | **Access point bring-up order (DEV-net-f; DEV-2, CH-7).** `BringUp` validates the configuration, starts `agentos-ap-exempt@<if>.service` (systemd-escaped by `ExemptUnit`) and only then calls `AccessPoint.Start`; a failed unit returns the error and the access point is not started. Rests on: the caller's `start` waits for the oneshot to finish (`systemctl start`), and the P2-1 loader calls `BringUp` rather than `Start`. | DEV-2, CH-7 | Wire `BringUp` into the P2-1 `agentos_ap` loader. |
+| L35 | **The claim screen (CTRL-claim).** With `Config.Claim` set, `/claim` takes the sticker code (a `?code=` link only fills the form in) and answers 422 with tries left for a wrong code, 423 with "restart me" when locked, and 409 "already claimed" after the claim. Setup routes and `/` wait for the claim and then admit only the claimant cookie. The usual CH-9 address, host and same-origin checks run first. See `broker/claim/ASSUMPTIONS.md` K6. | HW-10 | — |
